_exptl_special_details 
; 
#  Cell Mass                                 363.446
# Results of Mean Crystallite Size as determined using Bruker-AXS
# TOPAS Software based on the Scherrer Equation
#   Crystallite Size 
#      Cry size Lorentzian (nm)               94.0
#      Cry size Gaussian (nm)                 293.8
#      k:  1  LVol-IB (nm)                    56.370
#      k:  0.89  LVol-FWHM (nm)               76.259
#   Crystal Linear Absorption Coeff. (1/cm)   81.779
#   Crystal Density (g/cm^3^)                  2.630
#
#The Scherrer equation is used to relate the width of the diffraction peak
#(where fwhm is defined as the width of the peak at 1/2 maximum intensity)
#to the size of the crystallites, expressed as : D = 0.9?/?cos? where D is
#crystallite size in nm, ? is wavelength of XRD instrument, ? is the width
#of the peak at fwhm and ? is the Bragg angle of the peak.
;
